Changes from Version 1.2: this version protects the Work and its Outputs from
being used to build other models, and from misuse. This License is now
revocable: Quran-Lab may revoke it, for You or for everyone, and may change it,
at any time, with or without notice, and all rights not expressly granted are
reserved (Sections 2, 7, and 10). The Work and its Outputs may not be used to
train, fine-tune, distil, align, or otherwise develop a machine-learning model
without Quran-Lab's prior written permission (Section 14). A model that You
develop or control and that is evaluated, benchmarked, ranked, or compared using
the Work or its Outputs is a Derivative, and so is a model trained with that
permission; each must be available to everyone, free of charge, under this
License (Section 15). Outputs may be used only as Section 16 allows, chiefly to
provide the feature in which the Work runs. Bulk extraction, server-side or
batch inference without approval, circumventing protection or usage reporting,
and evading limits or blocks are forbidden (Section 17). TajweedFormer V4 and
later models, and other models Quran-Lab ships encrypted, are Protected Models,
usable only through Quran-Lab's SDK (Section 18). A Hosted Service now needs
Quran-Lab's written approval (Section 5), and Local Use means running the Work
on Your own device. When Your rights end, You must delete the Work, its Outputs,
and what You made from them (Section 10). Every new release is offered only
under the latest version of this License (Section 7). New sections cover
liability, indemnity, Quran-Lab's name, and remedies (Sections 11 and 20 to 22).
Running the Work in applications for learners, Local Use, and modifying or
porting the Work itself remain permitted (Section 19). Charging for the Work
remains prohibited, the condition still attaches to the Work and not to You, and
no attribution is required.

1. DEFINITIONS

   "You" means the individual or entity exercising rights under this License.

   "Quran-Lab" means the copyright holder named above, and any person or body,
   including a charitable trust, to which it transfers its rights in the Work.

   "Output" means anything produced by running the Work or a Derivative,
   including transcriptions, phonemes, labels, alignments, timings, scores,
   probabilities, logits, and embeddings, and any compilation of them or
   dataset, file, or artifact that contains them or is produced from them.

   "Train" means to train, pre-train, fine-tune, distil, align, adapt, or
   otherwise develop a machine-learning model, including by using data as
   training examples, as labels or targets, as a teacher, or as a reward or
   preference signal.

   "Protected Model" means TajweedFormer V4 and every later TajweedFormer model,
   and any other model that Quran-Lab distributes encrypted for use through its
   SDK, or designates as protected at the address from which it distributes the
   model or in the model's card. A model whose weights Quran-Lab publishes
   openly, such as the Zipformer models, is not a Protected Model.

   "Written permission" and "written approval" mean a statement in writing,
   including by email, sent by Quran-Lab, that names You and what it permits.
   Nothing else is permission or approval: not access to the Work, not the
   approval of an access request or a key, and not silence.

   "Derivative" means any work based on the Work, including:

   (a) any modification, fork, port, translation, format conversion,
       quantisation, or re-export of the Work, made without Training;

   (b) any dataset, lexicon, label set, file, or other artifact produced from
       the Work, from another Derivative, or, where Section 16 allows it, from
       Outputs;

   (c) any machine-learning model Trained using the Work or its Outputs with
       Quran-Lab's written permission under Section 14; and

   (d) any machine-learning model that You develop or control and that is
       evaluated, benchmarked, ranked, or compared using the Work or its
       Outputs, as Section 15 describes.

   A machine-learning model Trained using the Work or its Outputs without that
   permission is not a permitted Derivative, and making one breaches this
   License. Every condition this License places on a Derivative, including
   Sections 3, 7, and 10, still applies to such a model.

   "Charge" means requiring or accepting payment of any kind for the Work, for
   access to the Work, or for any feature, capability, or output that the Work
   provides. This includes sale, licensing for a fee, rental, a paid product or
   feature, a paid subscription, a paywall, a trial that later requires payment,
   and advertising revenue earned on a feature the Work powers.

   "Hosted Service" means running the Work or a Derivative for other people and
   giving them its Outputs over a network, for example through an API, a web
   application, or an inference endpoint. Distributing copies of the Work is not
   a Hosted Service.

   "Local Use" means running the Work or a Derivative on a personal device, such
   as a phone, tablet, or computer, that You or the person You teach or serve
   directly is using at that moment, for yourself or for that person, without
   making it available to other people over a network. A server, including a
   rented or remote server, is not a personal device, and processing
   recordings in bulk or in batches is not Local Use.

   "Cost Recovery" means charging the users of a Hosted Service no more than
   the actual, documented, strictly necessary direct costs of operating that
   service for those users, such as compute, storage, and bandwidth. Cost
   Recovery does not include any margin, markup, profit, salaries beyond
   direct operation, or overhead unrelated to running the service.

