15. MODELS THAT ARE DERIVATIVES ARE AVAILABLE TO EVERYONE

   Any machine-learning model that You develop or control, other than the Work
   itself and its modifications, ports, conversions, quantisations, and
   re-exports made without Training, and that is evaluated, benchmarked,
   ranked, or compared using the Work or its Outputs, is a Derivative. This
   includes using the Work or its Outputs as a reference, a judge, a baseline,
   or a source of scores, and including the model in a leaderboard or a
   published comparison that uses them. A model that You neither develop nor
   control, such as another party's model that appears in the same comparison,
   is not made a Derivative by this Section.

   You must make every model that is a Derivative under this Section or under
   Section 14 available to everyone, free of charge, under this License, at
   least in the way Quran-Lab makes its own models available:

   (a) any developer must be able to use the model, at no charge, through an
       SDK, a library, or a download;

   (b) the model must be offered under this License, with no additional or
       stricter terms; and

   (c) no one may be refused access to the model for not paying.

   The model's weights need not be published openly. The model may be
   protected, for example encrypted or licensed for each installation, as
   Quran-Lab's own models are, so long as anyone can obtain access to it free
   of charge and the conditions of this License pass on to everyone who uses
   it.

   You must do so no later than the first time any result of the evaluation,
   or any Output of a model Trained under Section 14, is shared with another
   person or published, and in any case within 30 days after the model is
   first evaluated or, for a model Trained under Section 14, within 30 days
   after its training ends. If You cannot do so for a model, You may not
   evaluate, benchmark, rank, or compare it using the Work or its Outputs.

16. OUTPUTS

   You may use Outputs only:

   (a) to provide, to the people who use it, the feature of the application or
       of the Local Use in which the Work runs;

   (b) to measure how well the Work itself performs; and

   (c) for an evaluation under Section 15, to the extent that evaluation needs
       them.

   You may not collect or retain Outputs in bulk, build a dataset from them, or
   transfer them to anyone, except as needed for one of these uses or with
   Quran-Lab's written permission. Keeping a learner's results for that
   learner's own progress, and sharing them with that learner or with that
   learner's teacher, is part of providing the feature.

17. PROHIBITED CONDUCT

   Whatever else this License permits, You may not, and may not permit or help
   another person to:

   (a) extract Outputs in bulk or by automated means, including by scripting,
       scraping, or driving an application that someone else has built on the
       Work;

   (b) run the Work or a Derivative on a server to process recordings for other
       people, or process recordings in bulk or in batches for any purpose other
       than measuring how well the Work itself performs (Section 19), without
       Quran-Lab's written approval;

   (c) circumvent, disable, or tamper with any protection, lease, attestation,
       key, rate limit, usage reporting, or telemetry that Quran-Lab or its
       software uses to deliver or protect the Work, or alter software so that
       it reports less or different usage than took place;

   (d) reverse engineer, decrypt, or extract a Protected Model, or the runtime
       that protects it (the Core), except to the extent the law allows this
       despite this restriction;

   (e) use more than one account, key, or identity to evade a limit, a review,
       or a decision of Quran-Lab;

   (f) register again, or use another person's account or key, after Quran-Lab
       has blocked or ended Your access, without its written permission; or

   (g) use the Work or its Outputs to build a machine-learning model that
       competes with the Work, except with Quran-Lab's written permission.
       Evaluating a model under Section 15 is not, by itself, building it.

   On Quran-Lab's reasonable request, You must explain in writing how You use
   the Work and its Outputs, and confirm that You comply with this License.

18. PROTECTED MODELS

   Whatever else this License permits, and unless Quran-Lab gives written
   permission, for example for an approved request for raw weights, You may use
   a Protected Model only through Quran-Lab's official SDK and its Core, as
   Quran-Lab distributes them, and You may not, and may not permit or help
   another person to:

   (a) extract, dump, decrypt, copy out, convert, re-host, repackage, bundle,
       or ship a Protected Model's files, or any part of them, inside an
       application or anywhere else;

   (b) load or run a Protected Model outside that SDK; or

   (c) interfere with how that SDK obtains, stores, or protects a Protected
       Model.

   A breach of this Section is a breach of this License, and Section 10 applies
   to it. This Section does not apply to a model whose weights Quran-Lab
   publishes openly, such as the Zipformer models; every other Section of this
   License does.

19. WHAT REMAINS PERMITTED

   The following remain permitted under this License, so long as they do
   nothing that Sections 14 to 18 forbid:

   (a) running the Work or a Derivative in an application for learners, on the
       learners' own devices, and, for a Protected Model, only through
       Quran-Lab's SDK, and using its Outputs within that application as Section
       16 allows;

   (b) Local Use;

   (c) modifying, porting, translating, converting, quantising, or
       re-exporting the Work itself, other than a Protected Model, without
       Training it, and distributing the result under Section 7; and

   (d) measuring how well the Work itself performs, where no other
       machine-learning model is evaluated, benchmarked, ranked, or compared.

